urn \"1\"\n- parseMulDiv returns \"1\"\n- parseAddSub: peek()=\"+\", advance to pos=3, calls parseMulDiv → parsePrimary: pos=3, peek()=\"2\", advance to pos=4, return \"2\"\n- evalArithmetic(\"1\", \"+\", \"2\") = \"3\"\n- peek() at pos=4 is \"\" (end of args), so parseAddSub returns \"3\"\n- Back in parsePrimary: peek() is \"\" which is != \")\", so error\n\nAt this point, the last consumed token was at pos=3 which is \"2\". So `args[pos-1]` = \"2\" which matches what gexpr reports. I can update the error message to reference that token directly. For the missing all case, gexpr includes the full path in its help message, which will vary by machine, so I need to normalize stderr by stripping those lines.\n\nI think the cleanest approach is fixing the unclosed paren error message and adding a normalizer that strips \"Try...\" lines for the missing_all case.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":34820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4199ce6e-af63-4a9e-a611-14ddfb03bfc2","uuid":"674e7ba5-3221-4d01-9fd5-4f3afe37ef6e"}
